\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Residual Slovene refusal rate for GaMS3-12B-Instruct as a function of two predictors. (a)\nobreakspace  {}Write-profile overlap $O_{\mathrm  {SL}}$: Spearman $\rho = -0.90$ ($p < 10^{-7}$); within energy levels, $\rho = -0.97$ (E2) and $\rho = -0.95$ (E3). Higher overlap with the causal write profile predicts lower residual refusal. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Raw depth of the edit (mean edited layer index): Spearman $\rho = -0.34$, $p = 0.15$ (not significant). Raw depth alone does not predict residual refusal; the overlap metric, which accounts for layer importance, is the informative predictor.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:depth-placement}{{3}{8}{Residual Slovene refusal rate for GaMS3-12B-Instruct as a function of two predictors. (a)~Write-profile overlap $O_{\mathrm {SL}}$: Spearman $\rho = -0.90$ ($p < 10^{-7}$); within energy levels, $\rho = -0.97$ (E2) and $\rho = -0.95$ (E3). Higher overlap with the causal write profile predicts lower residual refusal. (b)~Raw depth of the edit (mean edited layer index): Spearman $\rho = -0.34$, $p = 0.15$ (not significant). Raw depth alone does not predict residual refusal; the overlap metric, which accounts for layer importance, is the informative predictor}{figure.3}{}}
